 "statement": "NO DEMONSTRATED EDGE. Withholding the calls the macro qualifier was least confident in scores 0.4257 on the 66.2% of calls it kept, against 0.4212 for withholding the same number at random -- a difference of +0.0045 where 0.02 was required, and it wins 4 folds of 6 where 5 were required. The filter is not selecting the calls that were going to be right; it is selecting a subset, and a random subset of the same size does as well. Note also that full coverage scores 0.4226, so the direction model it is filtering has no edge of its own to concentrate -- this measures whether macro context adds decision quality, and the answer is that it does not.",
